{
  "_comment": "DIRECTION, KEYED ON LTCODE. Deciding direction from the line item's NAME, with a bare `return 'higher'` fallthrough, grades any cost line the lexicon misses as higher-is-better and prints a rising cost in house green: a utility's operations-and-maintenance line at $500.00M against $470.00M consensus would read as a beat (figures made up). A name can be wrong about its own metric: extending the regex with cost vocabulary flips EPS, EBIT and gross margin to lower-is-better, because 'Amortization' appears inside their exclusion clauses. A code cannot be wrong about itself, which is why this file exists and the lexicon is only a fallback.",
  "_contract": "Each entry is keyed on the BASE LTCODE and carries {polarity, label, aliases?, source, note?}. `polarity` is 'higher' | 'lower' | 'neutral' - the same three values resolve_metricset.py emits; this file never introduces a fourth. `label` is the line-item name the code carried when the entry was written, verbatim from the source: the lookup requires it to still match, so a code silently repurposed for a different metric falls back to the lexicon and warns rather than applying a stale direction. `source` records where the label came from. Derived suffixes -Y, -Q and -M inherit from their base code (a cost growing is bad, a cost as a share of revenue growing is bad). `source` and `note` are ADVISORY: no script reads them, and they are here so a future editor can see where a direction came from and why a contested one was accepted. `polarity`, `label` and `aliases` are the only fields polarity.py reads.",
  "_discipline": "Do NOT add a code whose label you cannot source from a live search_lineitem response or the package's own spec - a wrong entry defeats a correct regex silently and is worse than no entry. Add entries only after an A/B resolve of the corpus is green (internal edition only), declaring any intended move. Entries that merely confirm what the lexicon already resolves are wanted: they are what makes the silence legible, and they cost nothing because the harness proves they moved nothing.",
