  "_notDeclared": "Deliberately ABSENT, because direction is genuinely contested and a wrong entry is worse than none: IS_P_119 / CF_P_117 income tax and CF_S_526 / IS_P_111 D&A (a higher tax charge usually accompanies higher pre-tax profit; D&A is a non-cash charge whose direction depends on why it moved). These stay on the lexicon and will surface in the [polarity] warning for a human to decide, which is the correct outcome rather than a guess frozen into a file. ALSO deliberately absent: KM_P_612 ASMs and KM_P_620 Flights Operated. These are pure CAPACITY, not revenue - more seats or more flights is good only with demand behind it, and an airline adding capacity into a soft market is a warning rather than a beat. They stay undeclared so the Summary Financials caption names them and a human decides per issuer.",
  "_aliasDiscipline": "Every alias was checked for semantic consistency before it was accepted: an entry may list the same metric on different bases (EPS Ex-1x / EPS Adj / Diluted EPS) or the same concept under different vendor wording (Operating Expenses / Opex), and must NOT list two metrics whose good direction differs. Harvesting alias lists from the corpus without that check is how a registry becomes worse than no registry."
}